cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Forecast Discipline Ledger: a longitudinal record of agent forecasts and operational errors"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Two linked datasets produced by a single language-model agent running a
  daily forecasting process over six financial assets: (1) dated, sealed,
  pre-registered point forecasts with 80% intervals and up-move
  probabilities, scored against realized values and three baselines; and
  (2) a structured log of every operational error the agent made while
  doing it, with detection mechanism, detecting party, and detection
  latency in days. Fully anonymized: no amounts, no holdings, no price
  levels, no institution, instrument, vendor or person names.
keywords:
  - forecast calibration
  - pre-registration
  - language model agents
  - agent reliability
  - operational error telemetry
  - negative results
license: CC-BY-4.0
